","inline":true,"children":[{"text":"f_0=\frac{1-1}{x-1}=0"}]},{"text":" als untere Schranke nehmen. Die Obergrenze ist etwas schwieriger, auch da sie von "},{"type":"math","src":"x","inline":true,"children":[{"text":"x"}]},{"text":" abhängt. Wir kürzen zuerst einmal ein Minus aus unserer Formel:"}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"text":""},{"type":"math","src":"","inline":true,"children":[{"text":""}]},{"text":""},{"type":"math","src":"f_n = \frac{x^{n+1}-1}{x-1} = \frac{1-x^{n+1}}{1-x}","inline":true,"children":[{"text":""}]},{"text":"."}]},{"type":"p","children":[{"text":"Da "},{"type":"math","src":"0 < x < 1","inline":true,"children":[{"text":""}]},{"text":" nach Voraussetzungen gilt, ist "},{"type":"math","src":"1-x","inline":true,"children":[{"text":""}]},{"text":" positiv und "},{"type":"math","src":"-x^{n+1} ","inline":true,"children":[{"text":""}]},{"text":" immer negativ"},{"type":"math","src":"","inline":true,"children":[{"text":""}]},{"text":". Somit folgt: "},{"type":"math","src":"f_n = \frac{1-x^{n+1}}{1-x} < \frac{1}{1-x}","inline":true,"children":[{"text":""}]},{"text":", also ist "},{"type":"math","src":"\frac{1}{1-x}","inline":true,"children":[{"text":""}]},{"text":" eine obere Schranke. Somit ist "},{"type":"math","src":"(f_n)","inline":true,"children":[{"text":"(f_n)"}]},{"text":" (streng) monoton und beschränkt und daher konvergent. Der Grenzwert ist "},{"type":"math","src":"\frac{1}{1-x}
